{"name":"Young Turk","hex":"#c9afa9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Young Turk","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of young Turk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Young_Turk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Young Turks","blocks":[{"text":"The Young Turks were a broad opposition movement in the late Ottoman Empire to the absolutist régime of Sultan Abdul Hamid II. The prominent organisation within the movement was the Committee of Union and Progress, though its ideology, strategies, and membership continuously changed. By the 1890s, the Young Turks were mainly a loose and contentious network of exiled intelligentsia who made a living by selling their newspapers to secret subscribers. Beyond opposition, exiled writers and sociologists debated Turkey's place in the East–West dichotomy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Flag_of_the_Young_Turk_Revolution.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Young_Turk_Revolution.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_Turks"},{"title":"Turk (rapper)","blocks":[{"text":"Tab Virgil Jr. better known by his stage name Turk, is an American rapper from New Orleans, Louisiana. He is best known for his late 1990s run at Birdman's Cash Money Records with the group the Hot Boys."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/.Turk.jpg/330px-.Turk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turk_(rapper)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Greek_lithograph_celebrating_the_Ottoman_Constitution.png/500px-Greek_lithograph_celebrating_the_Ottoman_Constitution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Greek_lithograph_celebrating_the_Ottoman_Constitution.png/500px-Greek_lithograph_celebrating_the_Ottoman_Constitution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lithograph celebrating the Young Turk Revolution featuring the sources of inspiration of the movement, Midhat Pasha, Prince Sabahaddin, Deli Fuad Pasha and Namık Kemal, military leaders Niyazi Bey and Enver Pasha, and the slogan \"Liberty, equality, fraternity\" (hürriyet, müsavat, uhuvvet in Turkish, ελευθερία, ισότης, αδελφότης in Greek)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreek_lithograph_celebrating_the_Ottoman_Constitution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/1st_Young_Turk_Congress%2C_1902.jpg/500px-1st_Young_Turk_Congress%2C_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/1st_Young_Turk_Congress%2C_1902.jpg/1280px-1st_Young_Turk_Congress%2C_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/1st_Young_Turk_Congress%2C_1902.jpg/500px-1st_Young_Turk_Congress%2C_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young Turks who attended the congress held in Paris under the chairmanship of Prince Sabahattin between 4–9 February 1902","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1st_Young_Turk_Congress%2C_1902.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/First_Congress_of_the_Young_Turks_in_Paris_%281902%29.jpg/500px-First_Congress_of_the_Young_Turks_in_Paris_%281902%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/First_Congress_of_the_Young_Turks_in_Paris_%281902%29.jpg/1280px-First_Congress_of_the_Young_Turks_in_Paris_%281902%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe